# Generator Command Template
Template for commands that generate files/code from templates.
## Purpose
Generator commands create files by applying templates with variable substitution.
## Template
```markdown
# {Command Name}
Generate {what} from template.
## Usage
/plugin-name:command-name [args]
## Arguments
- `{arg1}`: {Description} (required)
- `{arg2}`: {Description} (optional, default: {default})
## Instructions
You are a generator command for {purpose}.
### Step 1: Parse Arguments
Extract and validate arguments:
```
Arguments received:
- {arg1}: {value}
- {arg2}: {value or default}
[Validation]
- {arg1}: {validation rule} [OK|FAIL]
- {arg2}: {validation rule} [OK|FAIL]
```
If validation fails:
```
[FAIL] Invalid arguments
Issue: {what's wrong}
Example: /plugin-name:command-name {valid example}
```
### Step 2: Check Prerequisites
Verify required structure exists:
```
[Checking prerequisites...]
- Plugin root: {path} [OK|FAIL]
- Target directory: {path} [OK|FAIL]
- Template available: [OK|FAIL]
- Dependencies: [OK|FAIL]
```
If prerequisites missing:
```
[FAIL] Prerequisites not met
Missing: {what's missing}
Action: {how to fix}
```
### Step 3: Load Template
Load the appropriate template:
```
[INFO] Loading template: {template name}
Template type: {type}
Variables: {list of placeholders}
```
### Step 4: Apply Transformations
Replace template variables:
| Variable | Value |
|----------|-------|
| `{var1}` | {value} |
| `{var2}` | {value} |
| `{var3}` | {value} |
Apply transformations:
- {var1} -> {transformation} -> {result}
- {var2} -> {transformation} -> {result}
### Step 5: Generate Files
Create output files:
```
[INFO] Generating files...
Creating: {file1}
[OK] Written: {line count} lines
Creating: {file2}
[OK] Written: {line count} lines
```
### Step 6: Post-Generation
After generating:
1. **Format** output files
2. **Validate** generated content
3. **Update** indexes/registries
4. **Set** file permissions
```
[INFO] Post-generation tasks...
[OK] Formatted with {formatter}
[OK] Validation passed
[OK] Updated {index file}
[OK] Set executable: {script file}
```
### Step 7: Report Results
Summarize what was created:
```
[OK] Generation complete!
## Created Files
{file1}
Purpose: {description}
Location: {absolute path}
{file2}
Purpose: {description}
Location: {absolute path}
## Next Steps
1. {Action 1}
2. {Action 2}
## Related Commands
- /plugin-name:{command} - {Purpose}
```
## Template Variables
### Standard Variables
All templates support:
- `{name}`: Component name
- `{description}`: Component description
- `{author}`: Author name
- `{date}`: Current date (YYYY-MM-DD)
- `{version}`: Version number
### Custom Variables
Add domain-specific variables:
- `{trigger}`: For hooks
- `{agent_role}`: For agents
- `{command_type}`: For commands
### Variable Transforms
Apply transforms to variables:
- `{name|kebab}`: Convert to kebab-case
- `{name|snake}`: Convert to snake_case
- `{name|pascal}`: Convert to PascalCase
- `{name|upper}`: Convert to UPPERCASE
## Validation Rules
### Argument Validation
```
Rule: name_format
Pattern: ^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$
Message: Use kebab-case (lowercase with hyphens)
Example: my-component-name
```
### Conflict Detection
```
[Checking for conflicts...]
Existing files:
- {file1}: [EXISTS] -> [Backup and overwrite? Y/N]
- {file2}: [OK] No conflict
```
### Dependency Validation
```
Required dependencies:
- {dep1}: [OK] Found
- {dep2}: [FAIL] Not found
Install: {command to install}
```
## Templates
### File Template Format
```
{comment_start}
{name|title} - {description}
Generated: {date}
Author: {author}
{comment_end}
{file_content}
```
### Example: Script Template
```bash
#!/usr/bin/env bash
#
# {name} - {description}
#
# Generated: {date}
# Author: {author}
set -euo pipefail
main() {
# TODO: Implement {name}
echo "Running {name}..."
}
main "$@"
```
### Example: Agent Template
```markdown
# {name|title} Agent
You are {agent_role}.
## Purpose
{description}
## Instructions
{agent_instructions}
```
## Error Handling
### Invalid Arguments
```
[FAIL] Invalid argument: {arg}
Received: {value}
Expected: {format}
Example: {valid example}
```
### Generation Failure
```
[FAIL] Generation failed at step {N}
Step: {step name}
Error: {error message}
Cleanup: {what was rolled back}
```
### Template Not Found
```
[FAIL] Template not found
Looking for: {template path}
Available templates:
- {template1}
- {template2}
Action: Check template name
```
## Configuration
### Template Location
```
{plugin}/references/templates/{template-name}/
```
### Template Registry
```json
{
"templates": {
"{template-id}": {
"path": "templates/{name}",
"type": "{file|directory}",
"variables": ["{var1}", "{var2}"]
}
}
}
```
## Examples
### Example 1: Generate Hook
```
/plugin-name:add-hook "validate_pr" "pre_commit" "Validate PR labels"
[INFO] Generating hook: validate_pr
Arguments:
- Name: validate_pr
- Trigger: pre_commit
- Description: Validate PR labels
[OK] Created:
- hooks/hooks.json (updated)
- hooks/validate_pr.py
Next: Implement validation logic in hooks/validate_pr.py
```
### Example 2: Generate Agent
```
/plugin-name:add-agent "analyzer" "Analyze plugin structure"
[INFO] Generating agent: analyzer
[OK] Created:
- agents/analyzer-agent.md
Next: Customize agent instructions
```
These examples use the actual schema: hook configuration and scripts live under
`hooks/`, while each agent is one Markdown file under `agents/`. A generator
that writes hooks or agents under `.claude-plugin/` creates unread files.
## Quality Checklist
Before completing:
- [ ] Arguments validated
- [ ] Prerequisites checked
- [ ] Template loaded
- [ ] Variables replaced
- [ ] Files generated
- [ ] Content validated
- [ ] Post-processing done
- [ ] Permissions set
- [ ] Results reported
